sysutils/proc-cli: import proc-cli-2.2.0

proc finds, inspects and stops processes and ports. Target a process by
port (:3000), PID, name or path, see what holds a port and why it is
there, and free it. Commands that change anything ask first, preview
with --dry-run, and print JSON with stable exit codes for scripts.

NetBSD is supported upstream since 2.2.0, whose CI runs the whole test
suite on NetBSD 11. Ports come from sockstat(1) and open files from
fstat(1), both in the base system, so it has no run dependencies.
